{"4699010": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Anatolian Horror Stories : Curse In Bayramdere", "steam_appid": 4699010, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "dlc": [4829330], "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >                               <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4699010/extras/8c3d936de993618a3692f33d83379817.avif?t=1787593660\" width=920 height=430 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Anatolian Horror Stories: Curse in Bayramdere is a third-person survival horror game that puts you in the shoes of an An ordinary young girl ,who receieves training at POMEM (Police Training Center ),facing extraordinary evil. No training. No special skills. Just the desperate need to find out what happened to the people she loves — and the will to survive long enough to do it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >                              <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4699010/extras/cb8a89da7ef4492413b708db06a870a8.avif?t=1787593660\" width=530 height=460 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A Village. A Disappearance. A Curse.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bayramdere looks like any other small Turkish village in Bursa. Elders sit outside in the evenings. Life moves slowly. At least that's what we thought.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tomris has no such patience. Her cousin is missing. And she is not leaving without answers.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >                               <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4699010/extras/7b1f904656d8b805f83e0b31e017b124.avif?t=1787593660\" width=518 height=350 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Key Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A Personal, Human Story</strong> — You are not a soldier or a detective. You are a university student alone in an unfamiliar village, driven by love for your family and the refusal to give up. That vulnerability makes every shadow feel closer and every danger feel real.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A Living Village With Dark Secrets</strong> — Bayramdere is not abandoned. Residents still go about their lives even as neighbors disappear one by one. Talk to the villagers to learn something</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Atmospheric Third-Person Survival Horror</strong> — Inspired by the classics of the genre, Curse in Bayramdere blends slow-burn dread with tense exploration and desperate combat encounters.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rooted in Anatolian Folklore</strong> — The curse haunting Bayramdere runs deeper than anyone dares admit. Drawn from the dark traditions of Turkish mythology, the evil here is ancient, patient, and unlike anything you have seen before.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Pistol Combat Under Pressure</strong> — Resources are scarce and the creatures stalking the village are relentless. Every bullet matters. Every decision matters. Know when to fight — and when to run.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Puzzle Solving Woven Into the World</strong> — Hidden caves to explore . Old family secrets buried in old newspaper pages. Ancient rituals hiding in plain sight. The truth about Bayramdere is all around you — if you can piece it together in time.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive Exploration</strong> — Search homes, fields and ruins hidden in the hills surrounding the village. Every corner of Bayramdere has a story. Some of them are still unfinished.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Authentically Turkish Setting</strong> — A richly detailed world built with genuine cultural atmosphere, bringing a fresh and deeply personal backdrop to the survival horror genre.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >P.S. It is my first game so any comments would be appreciated and will be read with great caution to make the game better.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >                               <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4699010/extras/8c3d936de993618a3692f33d83379817.avif?t=1787593660\" width=920 height=430 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Anatolian Horror Stories: Curse in Bayramdere is a third-person survival horror game that puts you in the shoes of an An ordinary young girl ,who receieves training at POMEM (Police Training Center ),facing extraordinary evil. No training. No special skills. Just the desperate need to find out what happened to the people she loves — and the will to survive long enough to do it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >                              <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4699010/extras/cb8a89da7ef4492413b708db06a870a8.avif?t=1787593660\" width=530 height=460 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A Village. A Disappearance. A Curse.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bayramdere looks like any other small Turkish village in Bursa. Elders sit outside in the evenings. Life moves slowly. At least that's what we thought.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tomris has no such patience. Her cousin is missing. And she is not leaving without answers.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >                               <span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4699010/extras/7b1f904656d8b805f83e0b31e017b124.avif?t=1787593660\" width=518 height=350 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Key Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A Personal, Human Story</strong> — You are not a soldier or a detective. You are a university student alone in an unfamiliar village, driven by love for your family and the refusal to give up. That vulnerability makes every shadow feel closer and every danger feel real.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A Living Village With Dark Secrets</strong> — Bayramdere is not abandoned. Residents still go about their lives even as neighbors disappear one by one. Talk to the villagers to learn something</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Atmospheric Third-Person Survival Horror</strong> — Inspired by the classics of the genre, Curse in Bayramdere blends slow-burn dread with tense exploration and desperate combat encounters.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rooted in Anatolian Folklore</strong> — The curse haunting Bayramdere runs deeper than anyone dares admit. Drawn from the dark traditions of Turkish mythology, the evil here is ancient, patient, and unlike anything you have seen before.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Pistol Combat Under Pressure</strong> — Resources are scarce and the creatures stalking the village are relentless. Every bullet matters. Every decision matters. Know when to fight — and when to run.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Puzzle Solving Woven Into the World</strong> — Hidden caves to explore . Old family secrets buried in old newspaper pages. Ancient rituals hiding in plain sight. The truth about Bayramdere is all around you — if you can piece it together in time.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive Exploration</strong> — Search homes, fields and ruins hidden in the hills surrounding the village. Every corner of Bayramdere has a story. Some of them are still unfinished.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Authentically Turkish Setting</strong> — A richly detailed world built with genuine cultural atmosphere, bringing a fresh and deeply personal backdrop to the survival horror genre.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >P.S. It is my first game so any comments would be appreciated and will be read with great caution to make the game better.</p>", "short_description": "Anatolian Horror Stories:Curse in Bayramdere is a third-person survival horror game that puts you in the shoes of an ordinary young woman facing an unknown evil.No special skills.Just the desperate need to find out what happened to the people she loves and the will to survive long enough to do it.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, French, Italian, German, Russian, Turkish, Spanish - Spain, Japanese<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4699010/12442dad131c7f15f4cee85d329ffe7c7c6c80be/header.jpg?t=1787593660", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4699010/912cc47a27c9a3f818ef2bf9e12facbcf2aa77a3/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1787593660", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4699010/912cc47a27c9a3f818ef2bf9e12facbcf2aa77a3/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1787593660", "website": "https://sites.google.com/view/tomrisecegames/ana-sayfa", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 64-bit<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel® Core™ i5-4460 or AMD FX™-6300 or better<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 8 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> NVIDIA® GeForce® GTX 960 or AMD Radeon™ RX 460<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 12<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 16 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> Any compatible sound card</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> 64-bit <br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i7-3770 or AMD FX-9590 o